/--
Direct compiler-backed certificate from a raw observer and bounded list-valued
local Bérard histories.

This is the most compact checked statement of the safe proof route.  The
external construction supplies:

* the raw reachable product observer;
* the non-initial handoff predicate;
* bounded local history lists and finite fringe selectors over the observer
  state;
* view decoders, output correctness, and reachable dynamic hierarchy.

